# Keep the shipped runtime libraries byte for byte.
#
# Git guesses whether a file is text and rewrites line endings in the ones it
# decides are. It guessed wrong about these: both Windows libraries lost a
# handful of bytes to that rewriting and stopped being loadable executables,
# and the only reason VR kept working was that the loader could not find them
# and quietly borrowed SteamVR's own copy instead.
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary

# The language files are read line by line as UTF-8 by the game itself, and a key is whatever
# precedes the first '=' on a line. Pinning them to LF keeps a checkout on Windows from putting
# a carriage return at the end of every value.
*.lang text eol=lf
